menu "Michi Music Stream Log"

    config MICHI_LOG_TAIL_SIZE_KB
        int "Tail ring buffer size (KB, PSRAM)"
        default 128
        range 16 1024
        help
          Size of the volatile log tail ring allocated from PSRAM at boot
          (the FIRST PSRAM allocation, so the address is deterministic
          across boots of the same build - the crash dump relies on it).
          Ring capacity is size/512 entries (512-byte slots; log payloads
          longer than 504 bytes are truncated in the tail only, the
          console is not). 128 KB = 255 entries.

    config MICHI_LOG_JOURNAL_MAX_KB
        int "Journal file max size (KB, SPIFFS)"
        default 256
        range 16 2048
        help
          Rotation threshold of journal.1: when it grows past this size it
          is renamed to journal.2 (the oldest file is dropped). Storage
          consumption is bounded by files * max (2 * 256 KB by default) on
          the SPIFFS "storage" partition (~8.25 MB).

    config MICHI_LOG_JOURNAL_FILES
        int "Journal files (rotation chain)"
        default 2
        range 1 4
        help
          Number of journal files in the rotation chain. 1 = single file
          that is truncated on rotation (no history); 2 = one generation
          of history; higher = more history at more SPIFFS space.

    config MICHI_LOG_CRASH_DUMP_KB
        int "Crash dump size (KB)"
        default 8
        range 2 64
        help
          How much of the previous boot's tail is copied to
          /spiffs/logs/crash_<boot_seq_prev>.txt after a crash reset
          (PANIC/INT_WDT/TASK_WDT/WDT) with a valid ring magic. Skipped
          (never invented) when the magic does not match. The dump keeps
          the NEWEST lines that fit: the ones just before the crash are
          the most valuable.

    config MICHI_LOG_CRASH_DUMP_KEEP
        int "Crash dumps kept on SPIFFS"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
          Number of crash_<seq>.txt files retained on the storage
          partition. When a new dump is written, the oldest dumps beyond
          this cap are deleted (the seq in the name orders them: highest
          seq = newest dump). Bounds the storage consumed by crash dumps
          to KEEP x max file size.

    config MICHI_LOG_QUEUE_LEN
        int "Journal event queue length"
        default 16
        range 4 256
        help
          Depth of the FreeRTOS queue between the FSM observer and the
          journal task. A full queue drops the event (counted, logged on
          the next drop). State changes and errors are rare (tens per
          day), so 16 is generous for a teardown storm.

    config MICHI_LOG_TAIL_MAX_ENTRIES_RESPONSE
        int "Maximum tail entries per /logs response"
        default 200
        range 50 500
        help
          Hard cap for the count query parameter of GET
          /api/v1/receiver/logs (handler default 100). Bounds the
          response size (each entry renders to at most ~519 bytes). The
          range is capped at 500: default 200; larger values spike
          internal-RAM cJSON usage (~130 KB at 200, ~1 MB at 2000) on
          top of the PSRAM entry buffers.

    config MICHI_LOG_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Journal task stack (bytes)"
        default 4096
        range 2048 16384
        help
          Stack of the journal task (SPIFFS open/append/close + rotation
          per event). The default is generous for the FILE* + snprintf
          frames.

endmenu
